From a0a456bf6f82b41fd083ef91802abdbe2965f7b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yu Dukai <646689853@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:54:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: waveshare-dsi-v2: Update Waveshare 5-DSI-TOUCH-A
 timing

On the Compute Module 4, the Waveshare 5-DSI-TOUCH-A panel lights up
correctly on DSI0 but fails to light up on DSI1 with the current
timing.

Update the display timing accordingly so that the panel also works on
DSI1: widen the horizontal sync pulse from 20 to 30 pixels. The
resulting 810x1324 pixel timing already reaches the required refresh
rate at the existing 70 MHz pixel clock, so the clock is left
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Yu Dukai <646689853@qq.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-waveshare-dsi-v2.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-waveshare-dsi-v2.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-waveshare-dsi-v2.c
@@ -2153,8 +2153,8 @@ static const struct drm_display_mode ws_
 	.clock = 70000,
 	.hdisplay = 720,
 	.hsync_start = 720 + 40,
-	.hsync_end = 720 + 40 + 20,
-	.htotal = 720 + 40 + 20 + 20,
+	.hsync_end = 720 + 40 + 30,
+	.htotal = 720 + 40 + 30 + 20,
 	.vdisplay = 1280,
 	.vsync_start = 1280 + 30,
 	.vsync_end = 1280 + 30 + 10,
